# Front Sass conventions

## Class names, not tags

Never select HTML tags in component styles. Add a class and style that.

```scss
// ❌ BAD
.icon {
  svg {
    width: 1.35rem;
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD
.iconSvg {
  width: 1.35rem;
}
```

Exception: global resets in `common/styles/base.scss` (`html`, `body`, form controls).

Pseudo-classes (`&:focus-visible`, `&:disabled`) and `::placeholder` are fine.

## BEM modifiers use one dash

Modifiers are a second class starting with `-`, nested as `&.-name`.

```scss
.TypographySmall {
  &.-bold {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
}

.field {
  &.-invalid {
    border-color: var(--color-danger);
  }
}
```

```tsx
className={[styles.field, invalid ? styles['-invalid'] : undefined].filter(Boolean).join(' ')}
```

Do not use `&.bold`, `&.fieldInvalid`, or `--` (`&--invalid`).

## Keep unused tokens

Never remove a custom property from `common/styles/tokens.scss` just because nothing references it yet.
